th problems and ways of staying healthy, and use them in a limited range of social situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le12ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Talking About Health Problems"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Explaining a Problem</span><br/>You can use the Simple Present tense in certain sentences to describe your health problems. <br/><br/>For example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">I am not feeling well. <br/>I have a cough. <br/>I have a bad back. <br/>I have a bad sunburn. <br/>I have a headache. <br/>I have a sore throat. <br/>I feel feverish. <br/>I have muscle cramps.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Symptoms</span><br/><br/>  When you see a doctor, he or she might ask, <span class=\"italic\">\u201cWhat are your symptoms?\u201d</span> <br/>Symptoms are feelings of illness or discomfort."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Modals Must vs. Should"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use the modals <span class=\"italic\">must</span>, <span class=\"italic\">have to </span> and <span class=\"italic\">should</span> to give recommendations. "}, {"type": "example", "content": " You must wear a shirt and put on sunblock when you are outside. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">must</span> and <span class=\"italic\">have to</span> to make very strong recommendations and to talk about necessity. <br/>  <span class=\"italic\">Should</span> is not as strong. It is a suggestion."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You should also drink lots of fluids and get some rest."}, {"type": "text", "content": "It is common to hear these types of suggestions at the doctor's office."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sunburn "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "red skin caused by exposure to the sun"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have a bad sunburn on my shoulders and back."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le12ob05aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about health problems."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sunstroke"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a health problem related to high body temperature"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Headache, fever and fatigue are all associated with sunstroke."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le12ob05aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "shoulder"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "part of the body that connects the arms to the torso"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have a bad sunburn on my shoulders and back."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le12ob05aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "feverish"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "feeling hot and weak"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I also have a headache and I feel feverish."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le12ob05aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "muscle cramps "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "pains in different muscles of your body"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Do you have muscle cramps?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le12ob05aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to be associated "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be connected to something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Headache, feeling feverish and muscle cramps are all associated with sunstroke. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le12ob05aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to avoid "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to stay away from"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I strongly suggest you avoid the sun for a few days."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le12ob05aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fluids"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "liquids you can drink (water, juice, etc.)"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You must get some rest and drink lots of fluids. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le12ob05aud02"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write a dialogue describing a health problem to your doctor."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Talk about the symptoms."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The doctor gives suggestions."}, {"type": "text", "content": " Practice your dialogue."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Change roles."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk about a health problem with a doctor."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I describe symptoms."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I ask for and receive suggestions."}]}], "type": "sena"}